"DESIGN/RESEARCH task. Today new_player hard-codes its starting allegiance via from_name(\"allegiance1\") (server/src/ecs_extension.rs). Instead, a new player's allegiance should be part of its entity blob. That requires a general way for an entity blob to specify STABLE LINKS -- and there are two distinct kinds that must be modeled separately: (1) references to long-lived EXTERNAL values: assets and already-existing long-lived entities (e.g. a shared allegiance entity, an asset id); and (2) references to entities generated DURING the blob's own creation batch -- the ids of related entities produced in the same instantiate pass (e.g. a container plus its inventory items that must point at each other). The blob format needs a stable, order-independent way to express both without relying on guessed/sequential entity ids. This is its own important design task; research options (named handles / local placeholders resolved at instantiation, symbolic asset references, a two-phase instantiate that assigns ids then resolves links, etc.) before implementing. Removing new_player's magic allegiance name is the motivating first use case."